---
// src/pages/uk-blue-staffy-puppy-buying-guide/index.astro — REBUILT from the approved board
// record (data/boards/uk-blue-staffy-puppy-buying-guide.json, approved 2026-09-20 and
// RE-APPROVED three times since for heading collisions with pages built after it).
// Hand-written and NOT regenerated by `npm run extract`: the slug is listed in
// data/facts/rebuilt.json, so `migration_parity.py` skips it and `facts_preserved_check.py`,
// `link_parity_check.py` and `verbatim_set_check.py` are its gates instead.
//
// THIS IS THE BUYING GUIDE, AND IT IS AN INSTRUMENT RATHER THAN A PITCH. `brief.strategy` is
// "the checklist you take to the visit": of the four pages scanned, the registry's gives
// twenty-two questions and no expected answers, the RSPCA and the PDSA cover puppy farms in
// prose with no table, and the veterinary blog gives six questions. Nobody pairs the question
// with the answer to listen for, and the migrated body already had all fifteen pairs written.
// So the fifteen questions and the eight-row red-flag comparison are the spine, and the rule
// the whole page is built on is that every test on it is meant to be applied to US as readily
// as to anybody else. That is also why the puppies and the prices arrive late, and why there
// is no urgency line anywhere: a page that spends two thousand words telling a reader that
// pressure is a warning sign cannot itself apply any.
//
// NO SELF-PRAISE BEYOND WHAT A FILE ON DISK CARRIES. The only claims made about this kennel
// are the ones data/settings.json, data/price-matrix.json, data/puppies.json and
// data/reviews.json hold, plus the two DNA clearances /blue-staffy-health-uk/ owns and this
// page LINKS rather than restates.
//
// WHAT THIS PAGE MAY NOT SAY, and none of it is an oversight (`brief.out_of_scope`):
// no £850 to £1,200 band and NONE of the migrated first-year budget — the vet, insurance,
// food, equipment, training and grooming ranges, the £1,970 to £3,870 total, the ongoing
// years and the emergency fund — because not one of those figures has a source on disk
// (Known Issue 11, `dropped.prices`); no BETH, KANE, ALIS or KOBE and none of their four
// prices, because data/puppies.json holds six different dogs; no health guarantee of any
// length (`guarantee_days: null`); no named testing laboratory; no former city; no location
// landing pages; no quiz, no calculator and no downloadable checklist (`brief.tool.pick` is
// none); no newsletter or waiting-list block; and NO FORM — the contact page carries the one
// form the form audit measures, and `talk-to-us` links it. The "five steps" headline figure
// was dropped as unbacked and is NOT reintroduced: the steps are named where the record names
// them and nowhere counted.
//
// KNOWN ISSUE 9 CLOSES ON THIS SECTION. `buying-steps` is where the buying process lives, and
// its H2 — "The Buying Process: How to Find the Perfect Blue Staffy Puppy in the UK" — is
// worded so it cannot collide with the homepage's "How to Buy Your Blue Staffy Puppy". The
// H3 under it that DID carry the colliding wording is `verbatim.changed`: it ends on "from Us".
//
// WORKING RULES 11 AND 14. All SEVENTEEN recorded images are carried at their original public
// paths with their original alt text, and the page's ONE embed is carried at its original id —
// `WuA0yo6HZKE`, mounted through `VideoEmbed` in the record's own `video-what-to-expect`
// section at the foot of the page, where the migrated body had it.
// `facts_preserved_check.py` reports by name any id a rebuilt page drops.
//
// WORKING RULE 15 (faithful rewrite). The VERBATIM SET is carried WORD FOR WORD and is READ
// OFF THE RECORD (`sections[].heading`, `sections[].verbatim_opening`, the tree nodes' own
// pair, `assets[].alt`, and the `data/faq.json` rows the record names) rather than retyped
// here, so a curly quote cannot drift between the record the breeder approved and the page
// that ships. FORTY-ONE deviations are recorded in `verbatim.changed` with their reasons —
// heading collisions, emoji glyphs, three alts the old theme truncated at a quote character,
// and the clauses rule 9 will not let a page assert. THE H1 IS NOT ONE OF THEM: `h1.pick` is
// variant 0, which IS the migrated H1 word for word, so no `h1` row is owed, none is written,
// and the slug's keyword phrase is already inside it ("UK Blue Staffy Puppy Buying Guide").
//
// THREE OF THOSE FORTY-ONE ARRIVED AFTER APPROVAL, which is why `approval.reapprovals` has
// three rows. /blue-staffy-uk-breeders/, /blue-staffy-health-uk/ and
// /uk-staffordshire-bull-terrier-guide/ were each built after this board was signed off, and
// each took a heading this record also held. The page that OWNS the subject keeps the wording
// and this one moves — the breed guide owns the daily exercise figure and the children-and-
// other-pets question, the health page owns the lifespan — so four H3s here are the re-approved
// wording rather than the migrated wording, and `heading()`/`node()` read the record either way.
//
// WORKING RULE 16. The hero is `H-GD3` — the text-led PANEL with the photo in a narrow column
// on the left and an aside beside the copy, in a card — and the counter is `C-GD2`, ring tiles
// beside the heading with the labels above them. /uk-staffordshire-bull-terrier-guide/ and
// /blue-staffy-health-uk/ share the hero id and take `C-GD3` and `C-GD1`; `C-GD2` is the third
// of the interior-guide trio and nobody else has it, which is exactly what the rule asks a
// layout family's three arrangements to be for. The recorded refresh delta for the hero is the
// CONTAINER: a text-led card, where the breed guide opens on a photograph.
//
// THE ASIDE IS THE RECORD'S OWN `hero.aside`, AND ONE OF ITS THREE ITEMS STATES A FIGURE. That
// item carries a `source` (amendment 10.6) and is therefore DERIVED here and checked against
// the wording the breeder approved: the "15" in "15 questions to ask the breeder" is counted
// off `sections[breeder-questions].table.rows` at build, and a table that has stopped holding
// fifteen rows stops the build rather than leaving the hero advertising a count the page below
// it does not keep. The other two items state nothing and are plain strings, which is also
// CHECKED rather than assumed — an item that had quietly started stating a figure would be a
// claim nobody derived. The three approved CHIPS are rendered in the same box as a single line,
// because `Hero` shows a chip row only for `ledge: 'chips'`: on H-GD3 the prop is handed over
// and dropped, and a claim the breeder approved is not worth losing to an arrangement. The FULL
// contents list is `PageNav`, which `PageShell` mounts from `sectionsFromRecord(record)` —
// twenty rows is far taller than the hero band.
//
// EVERY FIGURE IS DERIVED AND ASSERTED (amendment 10.5, and the lesson da9c34e wrote down).
// The record's `n` is a hand-written number, true on the day it was boarded. So the three
// counter tiles are COUNTED at build — the questions table's rows, the red-flag table's rows,
// and data/settings.json's deposit — and a reading that no longer matches what the breeder
// approved throws with both readings in the message. The `costs` table is the other direction:
// its four amounts are the record's own approved cells, and rather than retype them the page
// rebuilds each one from data/price-matrix.json and data/settings.json and refuses to build if
// a cell and its data file have stopped agreeing. NOTHING here types a price or a unit twice:
// the cell decides what prints and the assertion decides whether it may.
//
// TEN SECTIONS CARRY NO PICK. `buying-steps`, `temperament-fit`, `health-checks`,
// `eight-weeks`, `home-prep`, `socialisation`, `first-30-days`, `delivery`,
// `adoption-vs-buying` and `talk-to-us` have `options.pick: null`, so no arrangement was ever
// chosen for them and none is invented: they render with no `bl-box` class at all, exactly as
// the breed guide's eight no-pick sections do.
//
// WHERE A PICK AND A NOTE DISAGREE, THE PICK WINS — the lesson 8c71fcd wrote down about the
// health page's review block. Five sections here are in that position: `takeaways`,
// `breeder-questions`, `red-flags`, `questions` and `video-what-to-expect` each carry a
// `refresh.note` describing a different arrangement from the one `approval.picks` names. The
// note is the argument that was put to the breeder; the pick is the answer they gave. So the
// takeaways are the three-up grid on a band, the questions table is zebra rows in a card, the
// red-flag table takes the brass column rules, the FAQ sits beside its heading, and the video
// is a player in a card. Working rule 14 makes the facade the default "unless the breeder picks
// otherwise", and here they did.
//
// SCHEMA IS Article + VideoObject + FAQPage. `brief.schema.types` is WebPage + Article +
// FAQPage; BaseLayout already emits the `#webpage` node with the git-derived dates, so Article
// and FAQPage are minted here, and the VideoObject joins them because the page carries an
// embed and every embed on this site gets one (the correction ad7592d made). NO HowTo: the
// record does not ask for one, and a buying process described is not a recipe with a yield.
// THE ARTICLE CARRIES NO `dateModified`, deliberately: BaseLayout drops its own WebPage node
// the moment a page's schema mentions one (`selfDated`), and an Article whose `isPartOf` then
// pointed at a node nobody emitted is the dangling `@id` `schema_check.py` blocks on.
//
// H4-H6 ARE WRITTEN HERE, not in the record (amendment 2.1): the approved outline stops at the
// H3 the breeder read. Six ladders are written, which is what clears `min-h5-h6`'s floor of
// five each, and every ladder sentence traces to the migrated body, to this record or to a
// file under data/. The H6 lines all open on the record's own `tuple.h6_prefixes` entry,
// "Buyer Note:". Every heading renders through `titleCase()` (amendment 4b).
import PageShell from '../../layouts/PageShell.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/kit/Hero.astro';
import CounterStrip from '../../components/kit/CounterStrip.astro';
import DataTable from '../../components/kit/DataTable.astro';
import InfoCard from '../../components/kit/InfoCard.astro';
import VideoEmbed from '../../components/kit/VideoEmbed.astro';
import PuppyCard from '../../components/kit/PuppyCard.astro';
import Testimonial from '../../components/kit/Testimonial.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/kit/Faq.astro';
import BodyImage from '../../components/BodyImage.astro';
import { sectionsFromRecord } from '../../lib/sections';
import { pickedStyle, approvalInForce } from '../../lib/pickedStyle';
import { bakedAssets, bakedSrcset, inPublic } from '../../lib/assets';
import { recordText, countedFigures, numberWord, sourceKey, ledgeText,
  sentenceAnchor as S, type LedgeEntry, type StatRow } from '../../lib/recordText';
import { boxClass } from '../../lib/boardStyles';
import { titleCase as T } from '../../lib/headings';
import { loadFaq } from '../../lib/faq';
import { SITE, abs, gbp, type PuppyRow } from '../../lib/site';
import pageDates from '../../../data/page-dates.json';
import { videoObject } from '../../lib/video';
import puppiesJson from '../../../data/puppies.json';
import reviewsJson from '../../../data/reviews.json';
import settings from '../../../data/settings.json';
import prices from '../../../data/price-matrix.json';
import record from '../../../data/boards/uk-blue-staffy-puppy-buying-guide.json';

const path = '/uk-blue-staffy-puppy-buying-guide/';
const SLUG = 'uk-blue-staffy-puppy-buying-guide';
// The picked meta variants and H1, BY INDEX from the approval — never retyped here. The
// indices are read through a named check rather than through `!`: a non-null assertion is a
// promise to the type checker and nothing at all to the build, so an unapproved record would
// have rendered `undefined` into the `<title>`, the meta description and the H1 and shipped
// it. `board_gate.py` would have caught the record; nothing would have caught the page.
// The approval IN FORCE (spec §9 amendment 11a): the record went back to the board for its
// hero (Known Issues 30 and 35) with its approval carried under `approval_previous`, and what
// the page is called was never the question. `approvalInForce()` still throws for a record
// that has never been approved.
const approval = approvalInForce(record);
if (!approval.meta) {
  throw new Error(`${SLUG}: the approval in force names no title or description index — `
    + 'run scripts/board_approve.py before building the page');
}
const title = record.meta_set.titles[approval.meta.title];
const description = record.meta_set.descriptions[approval.meta.description];
const h1 = record.h1.variants[approval.h1];
for (const [what, value] of [['title', title], ['description', description], ['h1', h1]]) {
  if (!value) {
    throw new Error(`${SLUG}: the approval names a ${what} index the record has no variant `
      + 'for — the menu and the answer to it have stopped agreeing');
  }
}

// The seventeen migrated images, by slot, at their ORIGINAL public paths with the alt text the
// record baked (working rule 11; all seventeen alts are elements of the verbatim set). Three
// of them — the hero, the research photo and the training infographic — are the alts the
// record REPAIRED: the old theme closed each attribute early on a quote character inside the
// description, so a screen reader was read half a clause. A missing slot throws at build.
const asset = bakedAssets(record);
const stepsHero = asset('buy-steps-hero');
const research = asset('buy-research');
const transport = asset('buy-transport-process');
const familyBreeder = asset('buy-family-breeder');
const prosCons = asset('buy-pros-cons');
const maleRehoming = asset('buy-male-rehoming');
const healthWellbeing = asset('buy-health-wellbeing');
const vetCheck = asset('buy-vet-check');
const healthyLitter = asset('buy-healthy-litter');
const preparation = asset('buy-preparation');
const readyInfographic = asset('buy-ready-infographic');
const socialChecklist = asset('buy-socialisation-checklist');
const trainingSocial = asset('buy-training-socialisation');
const nationwide = asset('buy-nationwide');
const ukFamily = asset('buy-uk-family');
const adoptionInfographic = asset('buy-adoption-infographic');
const reviewsPhoto = asset('buy-reviews');

// The carried wording, read off the record rather than retyped (see the rule 15 note above).
const { sec, heading, opening, node, nodeOpening } = recordText(record);

/** One section's approved table block. The three tables on this page are `breeder-questions`
 *  (fifteen rows), `red-flags` (eight) and `costs` (four); two of the three are also what the
 *  counter counts, so they are data as well as layout. */
interface TableBlock { caption: string; columns: string[]; rows: string[][]; numeric?: number[] }
const tableOf = (id: string): TableBlock => {
  const t = (sec(id) as unknown as { table?: TableBlock }).table;
  if (!t) throw new Error(`${SLUG}: section ${id} carries no table`);
  return t;
};
const questionsTable = tableOf('breeder-questions');
const redFlagsTable = tableOf('red-flags');
const costsTable = tableOf('costs');

// THE REVIEW, BY NAME rather than by index. The record's intent states MODE: single on
// data/reviews.json entry 3 — Rachel L., London — because it is the one of the three that
// speaks to the buying PROCESS rather than to the dog: the health checks, the communication
// and the home-raised environment, which is what every section above it tells a reader to look
// for. WHICH review is the record's sentence inside `record_hash`; HOW the block is drawn is
// the pick.
interface Review { quote: string; name: string; place: string; source: string }
const rachel = (reviewsJson as Review[]).filter((r) => r.name === 'Rachel L.');
if (rachel.length !== 1) {
  throw new Error(`${SLUG}: data/reviews.json no longer holds the Rachel L. row the record names`);
}

// THE FOUR FAQ ROWS THE RECORD NAMES, BY ID, in the record's order. Three are sourced to this
// page — what to ask a breeder, how old a puppy should be, and how to tell an ethical breeder
// from a puppy farm — and the fourth, the deposit, is data/settings.json's. Every answer
// restates something the body above already says.
const faqSection = record.sections.find((s) => s.id === 'questions');
if (!faqSection) throw new Error(`${SLUG}: the record has no questions section to build the FAQ from`);
const faqRows = loadFaq();
const faqs = faqSection.tree.map((n) => {
  const row = faqRows.find((r) => r.id === n.heading);
  if (!row) throw new Error(`${SLUG}: data/faq.json has no row ${n.heading}`);
  return row;
});

// ── EVERY FIGURE, DERIVED FROM THE FILE ITS `source` NAMES ──────────────────────────────────
// Two kinds of source appear on this record: a row count of one of this page's own tables, and
// a scalar out of data/settings.json. `resolveFigure` is the ONE reader for both, so the hero
// aside and the counter strip cannot resolve the same citation two different ways — which is
// the whole point of the aside's first item and the counter's first tile citing one table.
const ROWS_OF = new RegExp(`^data/boards/${SLUG}\\.json#len\\(sections\\[([a-z0-9-]+)\\]\\.table\\.rows\\)$`);
const DEPOSIT_SOURCE = 'data/settings.json#deposit_gbp';
const resolveFigure = (source: string): string => {
  const m = ROWS_OF.exec(source);
  if (m) return String(tableOf(m[1]).rows.length);
  if (source === DEPOSIT_SOURCE) return `£${gbp(settings.deposit_gbp)}`;
  throw new Error(`${SLUG}: the figure cited as ${source} has no build-time derivation here — a `
    + 'number this page prints is read out of the file that holds it, never copied off the record');
};

// The three counter tiles. `countedFigures` throws with BOTH readings when a derived figure has
// stopped equalling the one the breeder approved: the data decides what prints, and the record
// decides when a human has to look at the board again.
const statRows = (sec('stats') as unknown as { stats: StatRow[] }).stats;
const COUNTED: Record<string, string> = Object.fromEntries(
  statRows.map((row) => [sourceKey(row.source), resolveFigure(String(row.source))]),
);
const counterStats = statRows.map(countedFigures(COUNTED, SLUG));

// THE COSTS TABLE, CHECKED AGAINST THE FILES THAT OWN ITS FOUR AMOUNTS. The cells are the
// breeder's approved wording and are rendered as approved; what is derived is the ANSWER each
// one should be giving, rebuilt from data/price-matrix.json and data/settings.json. A price
// that moves in the data and not on the board stops the build here rather than shipping a page
// that contradicts data/price-matrix.json, which is the file /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/ and
// every puppy card read. The cells are matched as a SET rather than row by row, so re-ordering
// the table on the board is not a silent way past this and dropping one is not either.
const expectedAmounts = new Set([
  `£${gbp(prices.male_gbp)}`,
  `£${gbp(prices.female_gbp)}`,
  `£${gbp(settings.deposit_gbp)}`,
  `£${gbp(settings.delivery_min_gbp)} to £${gbp(settings.delivery_max_gbp)}`,
]);
const printedAmounts = new Set(costsTable.rows.map((r) => String(r[1])));
for (const row of costsTable.rows) {
  if (!expectedAmounts.has(String(row[1]))) {
    throw new Error(`${SLUG}: the costs table prints "${row[1]}" for "${row[0]}", which is not one `
      + 'of the four amounts data/price-matrix.json and data/settings.json hold today '
      + `(${[...expectedAmounts].join(', ')}) — the board and the data have stopped agreeing`);
  }
}
if (printedAmounts.size !== expectedAmounts.size) {
  throw new Error(`${SLUG}: the costs table states ${printedAmounts.size} of the `
    + `${expectedAmounts.size} locked amounts — this is the only place on the page they appear, `
    + 'so one of them is now unstated');
}
if (!settings.deposit_refundable) {
  throw new Error(`${SLUG}: data/settings.json no longer records the deposit as refundable, and `
    + 'the costs table, the counter tile and the close all say it is');
}

// ── THE HERO'S OWN DATA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
const heroSection = sec('top') as unknown as
  { hero: { chips: LedgeEntry[]; aside: { title: string; items: LedgeEntry[] } } };
const heroChips = heroSection.hero.chips.map(ledgeText);
const heroAside = heroSection.hero.aside;
// ONE ITEM STATES A FIGURE AND IS DERIVED; THE OTHER TWO STATE NONE AND ARE CHECKED NOT TO.
// An item carrying a `source` owes a derivation (amendment 10.6), so its count is read out of
// the table it cites and the approved wording has to open on the same number. An item WITHOUT
// a source that had started stating a figure would be a claim nobody derived, which is the
// failure the other half of this loop exists to catch.
const HAS_DIGIT = /\d/;
const asideItems = heroAside.items.map((item) => {
  if (typeof item === 'string') {
    if (HAS_DIGIT.test(item)) {
      throw new Error(`${SLUG}: the hero aside item "${item}" states a figure and carries no `
        + 'source — an aside that has started making a claim needs deriving here rather than printing');
    }
    return item;
  }
  const source = (item as { text: string; source?: string }).source;
  if (!source) throw new Error(`${SLUG}: the hero aside item "${item.text}" is an object with no source`);
  const derived = resolveFigure(String(source));
  if (!item.text.startsWith(`${derived} `)) {
    throw new Error(`${SLUG}: the hero aside promises "${item.text}" and ${source} reads `
      + `${derived} today — the aside advertises a count the page below it no longer keeps`);
  }
  return item.text;
});

// The candidate list is built from the files that exist, not spelled into the markup: a
// hand-written `srcset` is a filename duplicated away from its file, and a 404 candidate is
// invisible to `img-srcset-within-2x` because the master is what paints. `inPublic` and
// `BODY_SIZES` are src/lib/assets.ts's — four rebuilt pages had written both for themselves.
// The panel hero paints its photo in a 224px column at 1280 and 144px between 1024 and 1199,
// and the 512px master alone decodes at 2.3x the wider of those. The 240 and 400 candidates
// baked BESIDE it (working rule 11: added, never in its place — the master is untouched, keeps
// its filename and is still the largest row) bring both readings inside 2x.
const heroSrcset = bakedSrcset(stepsHero, [240, 400], inPublic);
// NO BODY `srcset`. Every in-body master here is between 400px and 615px wide against a
// column that paints at about 420px, so the widest ratio on the page is 1.46x — inside
// `img-srcset-within-2x` on the master alone. Offering a candidate that is not on disk is the
// 404 `bakedSrcset` refuses to write.

const sections = sectionsFromRecord(record);
/** The git-derived dates BaseLayout reads for its WebPage node, for the Article to agree with. */
const articleDates = (pageDates.routes as Record<string, { datePublished: string }>)[path];

// Each section's approved arrangement, resolved through the same `boxClass()` the board preview
// called: what the breeder signed off is what ships. Only the ten sections that carry a pick
// are ever asked for one.
const style = (id: string) => pickedStyle(record, id);
const box = (id: string) => boxClass(style(id));
const heroStyle = style('top');
const counterStyle = style('stats');
const reviewStyle = style('owner-review');
const videoStyle = style('video-what-to-expect');

const video = (sec('video-what-to-expect') as unknown as
  { video: { id: string; title: string; caption: string } }).video;
const available = (puppiesJson as PuppyRow[]).filter((p) => p.status === 'Available');
const town = SITE.location_label.split(' · ')[0];
const hours = SITE.hours.replace('Mo-Su ', 'from ').replace('-', ' to ');
const delivery = `£${gbp(settings.delivery_min_gbp)} to £${gbp(settings.delivery_max_gbp)}`;
const deposit = `£${gbp(settings.deposit_gbp)}`;
// The two counts the prose states, off the same tables the counter counts rather than typed:
// the opening promises a number of questions and a number of warnings, and both are the
// length of a table further down this page. `questionWord` is the same count as a sentence
// writes it — the section label and the counter tile print the digit, the close prints the
// word, and all three are one reading of one table (the fix the 2026-09-21 review asked for:
// two hand-typed fifteens would have outlived the row that left the table).
const questionCount = String(questionsTable.rows.length);
const redFlagCount = String(redFlagsTable.rows.length);
const questionWord = numberWord(questionsTable.rows.length);

// THE PRICE SENTENCE NAMES THE DOGS DATA/PUPPIES.JSON HOLDS, not six names typed into a
// paragraph. The old spelling listed Roman, Byrd and Ince against one price and Vennie,
// Christa and Cheryl against the other, which is the litter written down twice — once in the
// data the grid renders and once in prose nobody would think to change when a puppy is
// reserved. The split is derived, and it is CHECKED: a price in data/puppies.json that has
// stopped matching data/price-matrix.json, or a sex with nobody in it, stops the build rather
// than printing a sentence the table two sections up contradicts.
const nameList = (rows: PuppyRow[]) => rows.map((r) => r.name).join(', ').replace(/, ([^,]*)$/, ' and $1');
const bySex = (sex: PuppyRow['sex'], expected: number) => {
  const rows = available.filter((p) => p.sex === sex);
  if (!rows.length) {
    throw new Error(`${SLUG}: data/puppies.json has no available ${sex} puppy, and the close `
      + 'names a price for one');
  }
  const wrong = rows.filter((r) => r.price_gbp !== expected);
  if (wrong.length) {
    throw new Error(`${SLUG}: ${wrong.map((r) => `${r.name} (£${r.price_gbp})`).join(', ')} `
      + `${wrong.length === 1 ? 'is' : 'are'} not at the £${expected} data/price-matrix.json `
      + `holds for a ${sex} — the close and the costs table would print two different prices`);
  }
  return nameList(rows);
};
const males = bySex('male', prices.male_gbp);
const females = bySex('female', prices.female_gbp);

// Article + VideoObject + FAQPage. The FAQPage is built from the SAME four rows the accordion
// renders; data/faq.json keeps the sentence-case wording, which is what `name` reads
// (amendment 6g). The VideoObject is built from the record's own `video` block through
// `src/lib/video.ts`, so the schema and the video sitemap describe one id in one spelling.
//
// `@id`s ARE ABSOLUTE, and the two REFERENCES are not, deliberately. The `isPartOf` and
// `mainEntityOfPage` pointers have to match the spelling of the node they point AT, and
// BaseLayout writes its WebPage `@id` relative (`/slug/#webpage`); a reference in the other
// spelling is the dangling `@id` `schema_check.py` blocks on.
const WEBPAGE = { '@id': `${path}#webpage` };
const pageSchema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    '@id': `${abs(path)}#article`,
    headline: h1,
    description,
    inLanguage: 'en-GB',
    // `datePublished` ONLY, git-derived, from the same map BaseLayout reads. No `dateModified`:
    // see the schema note in the header.
    ...(articleDates ? { datePublished: articleDates.datePublished } : {}),
    isPartOf: WEBPAGE,
    mainEntityOfPage: WEBPAGE,
    author: { '@id': `${abs('/')}#business` },
    publisher: { '@id': `${abs('/')}#business` },
  },
  videoObject(video, abs(path)),
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    '@id': `${abs(path)}#faq`,
    mainEntity: faqs.map((r) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: r.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: r.a },
    })),
  },
];
---
<PageShell
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={path}
  ogType="article"
  schema={pageSchema}
  sections={sections}
>
  {/* 01 top — hero, picked style H-GD3 (a text-led panel in a card: the photograph in a narrow
      column on the left, the copy beside it, the contents aside in a box of its own). The aside
      is a SLOT (amendment 8) and what goes in it is the record's own `hero.aside`, whose first
      item is derived above. No CTA buttons and no trust-chip row: the record gives the hero
      neither, and the arrangement's ledge is `aside` (amendment 6a). The recorded refresh delta
      is the CONTAINER — a text-led card, where the breed guide opens on a photograph. */}
  <section slot="hero" id="top" data-section-label="The buying guide" class={box('top')}>
    <Hero
      as="h1"
      eyebrow={`A UK breeder's buying guide · ${town}`}
      title={T(h1)}
      {/* ONE SENTENCE, ON ONE LINE, AND BOTH HALVES OF THAT ARE MEASURED.
          A SENTENCE: the lede used to be a noun phrase ("The questions to ask, and the answers
          to listen for") and a hero's lede is read aloud by a screen reader straight after the
          H1, where a fragment is a caption rather than a sentence. It has a finite verb now.
          ON ONE LINE, and that is the constraint the sentence had to be written inside. The
          picked H1 is the migrated one and it is 104 characters, so the title takes three lines
          in the panel's copy column where the breed guide's takes two, and the copy column has
          exactly one line of lede left before it grows the inner grid row past the 450px
          ceiling. `.hero-aside` is `align-self: center`, so a row taller than the band centres
          the aside in the overflow and the BOTTOM of it is clipped — `hero-aside-no-clip`,
          which fires at 1280 and which a screenshot does not show. Measured: one line of lede
          is 33px and leaves the aside 29px inside the band; two lines put it 4px outside. The
          desktop lede is also `-webkit-line-clamp: 2`, and a clamp HIDES its overflow, so a
          third line would disappear rather than push — invisible, and only a measurement finds
          it. The review asked for "This guide gives you the questions to ask a breeder, and the
          answers to listen for" and for it to be verified at one line: at 83 characters it
          measures two lines at 1024, 1100 and 1280 and puts the aside back outside the band, so
          this is the same sentence written to the measurement. */}
      lede="Here is what to ask a breeder, and what to listen for."
      image={stepsHero.file}
      imageAlt={stepsHero.alt}
      imageWidth={stepsHero.w}
      imageHeight={stepsHero.h}
      imageSrcset={heroSrcset}
      layout={heroStyle.layout.hero ?? 'panel'}
      align={heroStyle.layout.align ?? 'left'}
      media={heroStyle.layout.media ?? 'left'}
      ledge={heroStyle.layout.ledge ?? 'aside'}
    >
      {/* THE ASIDE IS THE PAGE'S MARKUP, and it carries the record's chips as well as its items.
          `Hero` renders the chip row only for `ledge: 'chips'` — correctly, because a hero
          showing two ledges is neither arrangement — so on H-GD3 the prop is handed over and
          dropped. The three chips are rendered here as a single line rather than a wrapped row,
          because a row costs the card two lines it does not have. */}
      <div slot="aside">
        <p class="aside-title">{heroAside.title}</p>
        <ul class="aside-items">
          {asideItems.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="aside-chips">{heroChips.join(' · ')}</p>
      </div>
    </Hero>
    <h2>{T(heading('top'))}</h2>
    <p>{opening('top')}</p>
    <h3>{T(node('top', 0).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('top', 0)}</p>
    <p>
      {questionCount} questions with the answer to listen for after each, and {redFlagCount}
      warnings that end a conversation.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* 02 takeaways — takeaways, picked style S2 (the three-up grid on a steel band, heading as an
      eyebrow). The section's own `refresh.note` argues for the rail of cards beside the heading,
      which is S3; `approval.picks` says S2, and the PICK beats the note. FOUR cards, which is
      what the record's tree carries, each the one-line form of a section below it — and each a
      claim the migrated body already makes or a file on disk already holds. */}
  <section id="takeaways" data-section-label="Four rules" class={box('takeaways')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('takeaways'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">Four things worth more than the rest.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <div class="bl-cards">
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T(node('takeaways', 0).heading)}
          body="If the dam is not in the room, there is no visit worth staying for. It is the clearest single signal on the whole list, and it costs nothing to check."
        />
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T(node('takeaways', 1).heading)}
          body="L-2-HGA and HC-HSF4, for both parents, on paper and in your hand. Told the parents are clear but shown no certificate, you have been told nothing you can check."
        />
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T(node('takeaways', 2).heading)}
          body="Eight weeks is the earliest a puppy leaves, here or anywhere. An offer to hand one over sooner tells you what that breeder is optimising for."
        />
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T(node('takeaways', 3).heading)}
          body="Get the terms in writing before any money moves. Cash with no paperwork and no receipt leaves you nothing to point at afterwards."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 03 stats — the counter strip, picked style C-GD2 (ring tiles beside the heading, each label
      above its figure): the interior-guide arrangement neither the breed guide nor the health
      page took, which is what keeps working rule 16's promise between three pages sharing a hero
      id. All three figures are counted at build — two off this page's own tables, one out of
      data/settings.json — and checked against the number the breeder approved. */}
  <section id="stats" data-section-label="What this guide gives you" class={box('stats')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('stats'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">Two lists and one figure, counted off the page itself.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <CounterStrip
        stats={counterStats}
        tiles={counterStyle.layout.tiles ?? 'ring'}
        label={counterStyle.layout.label ?? 'above'}
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 04 buying-steps — standard, and NO PICK: `options.pick` is null on this record, so no
      arrangement was ever chosen for it and none is invented here. THIS IS THE SECTION THAT
      CLOSES KNOWN ISSUE 9: the buying process lives on this page and the homepage keeps a
      different heading for it. The H2 and its opening are migrated wording, as are the first H3
      and its own opening — and that H3's ending, "from BlueStaffyUK.uk", is `verbatim.changed`
      and now reads "from Us". The steps are the migrated body's own and are named where the
      record names them; NO count of them is printed anywhere, because the "five steps" headline
      figure was dropped as unbacked and is not coming back. The recorded refresh delta is the
      LAYOUT. */}
  <section id="buying-steps" data-section-label="The buying process">
    <h2>{T(heading('buying-steps'))}</h2>
    <p>{opening('buying-steps')}</p>
    <BodyImage asset={research} />

    <h3>{T(node('buying-steps', 0).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('buying-steps', 0)}</p>
    <p>
      <a href="/">{S('Everything we do as breeders starts on our home page')}</a>, and every step
      below is one we will walk through with you at whatever pace you want to take it.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('buying-steps', 1).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      Look at the dogs that actually exist before you look at anything else. Each one has a page
      of its own with photographs, its sex, its price and whether it is still available, and the
      grid lower down this page is the same litter. Nothing is held back for a shortlist.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('buying-steps', 2).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      An email naming the puppy you are asking about, and a few lines about your household. There
      is no form on this page and no queue to join. Writing costs you nothing and holds nothing.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('buying-steps', 3).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      We ask who is at home and when, whether there are children or other animals, what the
      garden is like and how the dog will be exercised. This is not a formality and it is not
      always a yes.
      {' '}<a href="/blue-staffy-uk-breeders/">{S('Read who we are before you write to us')}</a> and
      you will know what a puppy is being matched against.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('buying-steps', 4).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      A deposit of {deposit} holds one named dog and is refundable. Nothing is reserved before
      that and nothing is reserved by a conversation. The balance is settled when the puppy goes.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('buying-steps', 5).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      {settings.delivery_note} — {delivery} — or collect in {town}. Either way the puppy leaves at
      eight weeks or later, microchipped, vet checked and with its first vaccination done.
      <a href="#talk-to-us">Ask us where you are in the process</a> at any point; we would rather
      answer twice than have you guess.
    </p>
    <BodyImage asset={transport} />

    <h4>{T('The Order Matters More Than The Speed')}</h4>
    <p>
      Every step before the deposit is reversible and costs nothing, which is deliberate. A
      process that asks for money early is a process that has stopped asking you questions.
    </p>
    <h5>{T('A Breeder Who Never Interviews You Is Not Choosing Anything')}</h5>
    <p>
      If nobody asks about your week, the only test being applied is whether your payment clears.
      That is worth noticing wherever you happen to be standing.
    </p>
    <h6>{T('Buyer Note: Ask what happens if you change your mind')}</h6>
    <p>Ours is refundable and the table below says so. Put the same question to anybody else before you send anything.</p>
  </section>

  {/* 05 breeder-questions — table, picked style S2 (zebra rows inside a card). The section's
      `refresh.note` argues for the brass column rules, which is S3; the PICK is S2 and the pick
      wins. FIFTEEN rows, each pairing the question with the answer to listen for — and the
      second column is the migrated body's own follow-up for each question, not an invention.
      This table is also DATA: the counter above counts its rows and so does the hero aside, so
      adding or removing one stops the build until the board has been looked at again. It stacks
      into labelled rows below 640px — `DataTable` carries `.stack-table` unconditionally
      (working rule 13). The H2 is `verbatim.changed`: the paw glyph is gone and nothing else
      moved. The recorded refresh delta is the ACCENT. */}
  <section id="breeder-questions" data-section-label={`${questionCount} questions to ask`} class={box('breeder-questions')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('breeder-questions'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">{opening('breeder-questions')}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <h3>{T(node('breeder-questions', 0).heading)}</h3>
      <p>{nodeOpening('breeder-questions', 0)}</p>
      <BodyImage asset={familyBreeder} />
      <DataTable
        caption={questionsTable.caption}
        columns={questionsTable.columns}
        rows={questionsTable.rows}
      />

      <h3>{T(node('breeder-questions', 1).heading)}</h3>
      <p>
        Work down it out loud, in order. You are not being rude, and nobody worth buying from will
        think you are.
        {' '}<a href="https://www.royalkennelclub.com/your-dog/getting-a-dog/buying-a-dog/questions-for-the-breeder/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{S("the registry's own questions to ask a breeder")}</a> is
        a longer list written by people with no puppies to sell, and it is worth reading beside
        this one. <a href="#talk-to-us">Put these to us first</a> if you would rather practise on
        somebody who has invited it.
      </p>

      <h4>{T('The Second Column Is The Point Of The Table')}</h4>
      <p>
        Anybody can ask a question. Knowing what a good answer sounds like is what turns the
        asking into a decision, and it is the part every other checklist we read leaves out.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('A Dodged Question Is An Answer')}</h5>
      <p>
        You are entitled to ask and nobody is obliged to answer. What a breeder will not put in
        front of you, after a polite request, tells you more about that afternoon than everything
        they did put in front of you.
      </p>
      <h6>{T('Buyer Note: Print it rather than reading it off a phone')}</h6>
      <p>A sheet of paper in your hand is harder to abandon halfway down than a screen is, with a puppy in your lap.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 06 red-flags — table, picked style S3 (borderless rows with brass column rules). The
      section's `refresh.note` argues for zebra rows in a card, which is S2; the PICK is S3. The
      migrated page's comparison, kept as a table: eight topics, what an ethical breeder does and
      what a dealer does instead. Every cell is the migrated body's own wording as plain
      sentences. THE OPENING IS `verbatim.changed`: "Thousands of UK buyers unknowingly buy from
      puppy farms each year" is a national figure with no source on disk and none this business
      could give, so it is gone and the sentence that says what the table is for is carried word
      for word. The H2 is changed too — the red-flag glyph, and nothing else. These eight rows
      are the counter's second tile. The recorded refresh delta is the MOTIF. */}
  <section id="red-flags" data-section-label="Ethical breeder or puppy farm" class={box('red-flags')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('red-flags'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">{opening('red-flags')}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <DataTable
        caption={redFlagsTable.caption}
        columns={redFlagsTable.columns}
        rows={redFlagsTable.rows}
      />

      <h3>{T(node('red-flags', 0).heading)}</h3>
      <p>
        These are not a score to add up. Any single row of the right-hand column is reason enough
        to leave, and the meeting place and the missing mother are the two that usually come
        first. A reputable breeder sits on the left of every row and will not mind you checking.
        {' '}<a href="https://www.rspca.org.uk/adviceandwelfare/pets/dogs/puppy/sales" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{S("the RSPCA's guide to spotting a puppy dealer's advert")}</a> covers
        the same ground from the charity's side, written by people with nothing to sell you.
      </p>

      <h4>{T('Walking Away Costs You An Afternoon')}</h4>
      <p>
        Staying costs a great deal more, and the pressure not to leave is usually the point of the
        pressure. There will be another litter.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('Reporting It Is Worth The Ten Minutes')}</h5>
      <p>
        A dealer who loses one sale carries on regardless. The charity above takes reports, and an
        advert that gets pulled is one family who never made the trip.
      </p>
      <h6>{T('Buyer Note: A car park is not a compromise')}</h6>
      <p>It is the whole red flag. Where you are asked to meet is the first row of the table for a reason.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 07 costs — table, picked style S1 (ruled rows under a brand header band), which is what the
      section's refresh note asks for as well. THE ONLY COST FIGURES ON THIS PAGE, and all four
      come from locked data: the two prices out of data/price-matrix.json and the deposit and the
      delivery band out of data/settings.json. Every cell is checked against its file at build
      above. NOT ONE figure of the migrated first-year budget is restated anywhere — the £850 to
      £1,200 band, the vet, insurance, food, equipment, training and grooming ranges and the
      £1,970 to £3,870 total are all `dropped.prices`, and the second H3 says so in as many
      words. The long first H3 is `verbatim.changed` (the abbreviation is written out to break a
      collision with the health page) and so is its opening, which carried the old band. The
      recorded refresh delta is the ACCENT. */}
  <section id="costs" data-section-label="What a puppy costs" class={box('costs')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('costs'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">Four figures, and every one of them is on a file we keep.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <DataTable
        caption={costsTable.caption}
        columns={costsTable.columns}
        rows={costsTable.rows}
        numeric={costsTable.numeric}
      />

      <h3>{T(node('costs', 0).heading)}</h3>
      <p>{nodeOpening('costs', 0)}</p>
      <p>
        <a href="/blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/">{S('See what is included in the price and how delivery is worked out')}</a>,
        which is where the same four figures are set out against what each one buys.
      </p>

      <h3>{T(node('costs', 1).heading)}</h3>
      <p>
        The old version of this page carried a full first-year budget: vet bills, insurance, food,
        equipment, classes, grooming and a total built out of them. Nobody here worked those out
        and nobody here can check them, so they are gone rather than rounded. Your own vet and
        your own insurer will quote you for your own dog, and those two figures are worth more
        than any range we could print.
      </p>

      <h3>{T(node('costs', 2).heading)}</h3>
      <p>
        {deposit} takes one named dog off the list, and it is refundable. It is not a fee for
        being considered, it does not buy a place in a queue, and it is paid after we have talked
        rather than before. <a href="#talk-to-us">Ask us about it before you send anything</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 08 temperament-fit — standard, NO PICK. The honest fit check, before anyone pays anything.
      All five H3s and all five of their openings are migrated wording, and TWO of the five
      headings are `verbatim.changed` by the third re-approval: the breed guide, built after this
      board was approved, renders data/faq.json's daily-exercise and children-and-other-pets
      rows, both elements of ITS verbatim set, and the two five-word shingles failed against
      them. The breed guide owns the exercise figure and the children question; this page owns
      buying, so the wording moved here and every subject word was kept. The drawbacks are stated
      as plainly as the advantages, six of each, which is the migrated body's own pros-and-cons
      table written out as prose. The recorded refresh delta is the LAYOUT. */}
  <section id="temperament-fit" data-section-label="Is the breed right for you">
    <h2>{T(heading('temperament-fit'))}</h2>
    <p>{opening('temperament-fit')}</p>
    <BodyImage asset={prosCons} />

    <h3>{T(node('temperament-fit', 0).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('temperament-fit', 0)}</p>
    <p>
      Historically bred for courage, they are fearless and determined, and a well-bred one
      socialised early directs that appropriately. They are smart and eager to learn too,
      responding well to positive reinforcement training kept consistent by everybody.
      {' '}<a href="/uk-staffordshire-bull-terrier-guide/">{S('Our breed guide covers the temperament, the history and the law in full')}</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('temperament-fit', 1).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('temperament-fit', 1)}</p>

    <h3>{T(node('temperament-fit', 2).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('temperament-fit', 2)}</p>

    <h3>{T(node('temperament-fit', 3).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('temperament-fit', 3)}</p>
    <p>
      Six advantages and six drawbacks; the second six matter more.
      {' '}<a href="https://www.pdsa.org.uk/pet-help-and-advice/looking-after-your-pet/puppies-dogs/medium-dogs/staffordshire-bull-terrier" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{S("the PDSA's veterinary view of what living with a Staffy involves")}</a> has
      a vet behind it.
    </p>
    <BodyImage asset={maleRehoming} />

    <h3>{T(node('temperament-fit', 4).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('temperament-fit', 4)}</p>
    <p>
      The one household we talk people out of is the empty one.
      <a href="#talk-to-us">Tell us about your week</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* 09 health-checks — standard, NO PICK. What to ask for, and what to look at. The two DNA
      tests by name and nothing beyond them: two is the number of DNA screens this breed has, and
      a third named on a breeder's site is a credential nobody can check. Then the seven things
      to look at on the puppy in front of you, which are the migrated body's own list. Our own
      parents are stated as clear, and /blue-staffy-health-uk/ is where the results live — a
      second page reproducing that table would be two pages claiming one set of certificates.
      NO LABORATORY IS NAMED (`dropped.names`), no prevalence figure, no percentage and no
      prognosis. THE OPENING IS `verbatim.changed`: "and our puppy health guarantees" promises a
      document with a length data/settings.json does not hold. Two of the five H3s are changed as
      well, both for collisions with the health page. The recorded refresh delta is the LAYOUT. */}
  <section id="health-checks" data-section-label="Health evidence to ask for">
    <h2>{T(heading('health-checks'))}</h2>
    <BodyImage asset={healthWellbeing} />
    <p>{opening('health-checks')}</p>

    <h3>{T(node('health-checks', 0).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('health-checks', 0)}</p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://www.royalkennelclub.com/health-and-dog-care/health-dog-care/health/getting-started-with-health-testing-and-screening/dna-testing/dna-test-l-2hga/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{S("the registry's own page on the L-2-HGA DNA test")}</a> explains
      the first, and
      {' '}<a href="https://www.royalkennelclub.com/health-and-dog-care/health-dog-care/health/getting-started-with-health-testing-and-screening/dna-testing/dna-test-hc-hsf4/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the registry's own page on the HC-HSF4 DNA test</a> the
      second. Two questions cover it: what health tests have the parents undergone, and can I see
      the certificates? Ask to hold the paper, and check the name on it against the dog.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('health-checks', 1).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('health-checks', 1)}</p>
    <p>
      L-2-hydroxyglutaric aciduria is neurological and affects coordination and gait; HC-HSF4 is
      hereditary cataracts, and takes the sight. Both are avoidable in a litter whose parents were
      screened before mating.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('health-checks', 2).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('health-checks', 2)}</p>
    <p>
      Seven things, and none needs a vet beside you. Bright, clear eyes, no discharge or redness.
      Clean ears, no heavy wax or odour. A clean, moist nose. Good body condition, neither thin
      nor bloated. Alert and playful, not timid or snappy. A clean rear end. Good mobility, no
      limping or stiffness. One failure is a question to ask out loud, not a verdict.
    </p>
    <BodyImage asset={vetCheck} />

    <h3>{T(node('health-checks', 3).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      Both ours are recorded clear of both. That is the only sentence here about our own dogs.
      {' '}<a href="/blue-staffy-health-uk/">{S('Our health page states what both parents were tested for and what the results were')}</a>,
      against the dogs they belong to. No laboratory is named there or here: no file we keep
      records one.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('health-checks', 4).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('health-checks', 4)}</p>
    <p>
      Beyond those two, skin irritation and joint wear are what the vet sees most. Neither is
      given a percentage here: we hold no prevalence data, and a figure invented to sound
      authoritative is the fabrication this page warns about.
      {' '}<a href="#talk-to-us">Ask us to see the certificates</a> first.
    </p>

    <h4>{T('Two Tests, And Only Two')}</h4>
    <p>
      A breeder listing four or five DNA screens for this breed is listing tests that do not exist
      for it. That is worth knowing before somebody impresses you with a longer list than ours.
    </p>
    <h5>{T('Clear To Clear Is The Pairing To Ask About')}</h5>
    <p>
      Carrier to clear produces no affected puppies either; carrier to carrier can. The table above
      says so in one row, and it is the row most buyers skip.
    </p>
    <h6>{T('Buyer Note: A certificate belongs to a dog, not to a kennel')}</h6>
    <p>A house rule is not a result. Read the name printed on the paper, and make sure it is the animal you were shown.</p>
  </section>

  {/* 10 eight-weeks — standard, NO PICK. The one date in the whole process that is not
      negotiable. The H2 and its opening are migrated wording; the H2 is `verbatim.changed`,
      with "bring a blue Staffy puppy home" reordered to "bring home a blue Staffy puppy" to
      break a collision with a location page, which keeps all five words. The recorded refresh
      delta is the CONTAINER. */}
  <section id="eight-weeks" data-section-label="Why eight weeks">
    <h2>{T(heading('eight-weeks'))}</h2>
    <p>{opening('eight-weeks')}</p>
    <BodyImage asset={healthyLitter} />

    <h3>{T(node('eight-weeks', 0).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      Bite inhibition comes from littermates who yelp and stop playing, not from a person saying
      no. Boundaries come from a mother out of patience. Reading another dog comes from getting
      it wrong somewhere safe. None of the three is taught as well afterwards.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('eight-weeks', 1).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      A puppy taken early is more likely to be anxious, more likely to mouth too hard, and more
      likely to struggle with other dogs later. The cost is not paid in the first fortnight; it is
      paid over years, by a family who cannot work out where the behaviour came from.
      {' '}<a href="https://www.rspca.org.uk/adviceandwelfare/pets/dogs/puppy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{S("the RSPCA's independent advice on a puppy's first weeks")}</a> sets
      out the same window without a litter to place.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('eight-weeks', 2).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      An offer to let a puppy go at six or seven weeks is a breeder telling you what they are
      optimising for, and it is not the dog. Ours go at eight weeks or later, and we hold one back
      longer if it is not ready.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* 11 home-prep — standard, NO PICK. What to do and what to buy before the puppy arrives. The
      H2 and its opening are migrated wording, as are the third H3 and its own opening — whose
      "premium Royal Canin dog food and" is `verbatim.changed`, because naming a manufacturer is
      naming a brand no file on disk records and the words linked to that manufacturer's shop
      (`dropped.names`, `dropped.links`). NO BRAND IS NAMED HERE. The recorded refresh delta is
      the DENSITY. */}
  <section id="home-prep" data-section-label="Preparing your home">
    <h2>{T(heading('home-prep'))}</h2>
    <p>{opening('home-prep')}</p>
    <BodyImage asset={preparation} />

    <h3>{T(node('home-prep', 0).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      Cables secured, cleaning products and medicines behind a door that shuts, toxic houseplants
      out, and a gate across anything better left uninvestigated at three in the morning. Do it
      the week before.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('home-prep', 1).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      A crate or bed in one quiet indoor corner, out of the through-traffic but not shut away,
      with something in it that smells of you. Somewhere to retreat to settles a dog faster.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('home-prep', 2).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('home-prep', 2)}</p>
    <p>
      Bowls, a collar and lead, toys tough enough for a chewer, a brush, bedding, flea and worm
      treatment, and a crate or pen. No brand is named: no file we keep records one, and whatever
      has been fed here is what to carry on with.
      {' '}<a href="/blue-staffy-blog-guides/">{S('Our blog guides go further on the first weeks at home')}</a>.
    </p>
    <BodyImage asset={readyInfographic} />

    <h3>{T(node('home-prep', 3).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      Pick the spot before arrival and use the same route every time: after waking, after eating,
      after play. Praise it outdoors; clean up indoors without a word.
      <a href="#talk-to-us">Ask us what your puppy is used to</a> and the routine is half-built
      already.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* 12 socialisation — standard, NO PICK. The three months that decide what kind of adult dog
      you have, then the vaccination course, then feeding. The H2 and its opening are migrated
      wording; the opening is `verbatim.changed` twice over — a promise of a downloadable
      checklist that does not exist comes out, and "stffy" is a misspelling of the breed's own
      short name rather than a wording, so it is corrected rather than shipped. The food H3 is
      changed for a collision with the homepage. WE GIVE THE FIRST VACCINATION AND THE OWNER'S
      VET COMPLETES THE COURSE; no schedule beyond the migrated body's own is printed. The
      recorded refresh delta is the ACCENT. */}
  <section id="socialisation" data-section-label="Socialisation and vaccinations">
    <h2>{T(heading('socialisation'))}</h2>
    <p>{opening('socialisation')}</p>
    <BodyImage asset={socialChecklist} />

    <h3>{T(node('socialisation', 0).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('socialisation', 0)}</p>
    <p>
      Sights, sounds, surfaces and people in small positive doses, never to the point of fright;
      other dogs only once vaccinated. One carried out to watch traffic is being socialised.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('socialisation', 1).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      Enrolling in local puppy socialisation classes is worth doing before you collect: the good
      ones fill. Concentrating with other dogs in the room is a different skill from concentrating
      in your kitchen, and it is the one that matters on a pavement.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('socialisation', 2).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      Ears, paws, mouth and tail, daily, by everyone. Do it now and a vet visit is an
      inconvenience; skip it and a nail trim is a decade of wrestling.
    </p>
    <BodyImage asset={trainingSocial} />

    <h3>{T(node('socialisation', 3).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('socialisation', 3)}</p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://www.pdsa.org.uk/pet-help-and-advice/pet-health-hub/other-veterinary-advice/dog-vaccines" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{S("the PDSA's guide to the vaccination course")}</a> sets
      out the second dose and the booster, both your own vet's rather than ours.
      <a href="#talk-to-us">Ask us what has already been given</a> and it goes in writing with the
      paperwork.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('socialisation', 4).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('socialisation', 4)}</p>
  </section>

  {/* 13 first-30-days — standard, NO PICK. The migrated page's four-week plan, kept because it
      is the most useful thing on the old page. The H2 is `verbatim.changed` for its clipboard
      glyph and nothing else. Every instruction here is the migrated body's own; no meal count,
      no worming interval and no visit frequency is added to it. The recorded refresh delta is
      the MOTIF. */}
  <section id="first-30-days" data-section-label="Your first 30 days">
    <h2>{T(heading('first-30-days'))}</h2>
    <p>{opening('first-30-days')}</p>

    <h3>{T(node('first-30-days', 0).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      Keep the house calm and the visitors down for the first few days. Set the crate up in a
      quiet corner with something of yours in it. Feed exactly what the puppy has been eating
      here, for at least the first week. Start the toilet routine straight away — outside every
      couple of hours and after every meal. Register with a local vet within forty-eight hours,
      and book the second vaccination while you are on the phone to them.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('first-30-days', 1).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      Name recognition in short sessions, a few times a day rather than one long one. The first
      command, taught with rewards and nothing else. Handling exercises for ears, paws and mouth.
      Carry the puppy outdoors to hear the world before the vaccination course is finished. And
      get the insurance in place, with cover starting the day the puppy arrives.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('first-30-days', 2).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      Once the course is complete, controlled walks begin — short ones, built up gradually rather
      than a mile on the first afternoon. Introductions to vaccinated, friendly adult dogs.
      Traffic, children and cyclists met positively and at a distance. Book the training class,
      and start on leaving things alone and coming back when called.
      {' '}<a href="https://www.gov.uk/get-your-dog-cat-microchipped" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{S("the government's guidance on transferring the microchip details")}</a> is
      the job most new owners forget in this week: the chip is already in, and the record has to
      be moved into your name.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('first-30-days', 3).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      The first class attended rather than only booked. Time alone introduced deliberately,
      starting at a few minutes and building across the month, so that being left is ordinary
      before it ever has to be long. A weigh-in, with the food adjusted to it. And short, positive
      car journeys that end somewhere good.
    </p>

    <h4>{T('The Month Is A Shape, Not A Schedule')}</h4>
    <p>
      Your puppy has not read it. Move a week if you need to; the order is what matters, because
      each week is what makes the next one possible.
    </p>
    <h5>{T('Alone Time Is The One Most People Start Too Late')}</h5>
    <p>
      A breed this attached to its people will not learn it by accident, and week four is not too
      early. Five minutes at a time, while the house is still calm.
    </p>
    <h6>{T('Buyer Note: Keep the breeder on the end of a phone')}</h6>
    <p>The first month is when the small questions arrive. Ask them here rather than searching for an answer at midnight.</p>
  </section>

  {/* 14 delivery — standard, NO PICK. The two ways a puppy leaves: collection here, or UK home
      delivery by DEFRA-approved transport at the band data/settings.json holds. The H2 is
      `verbatim.changed` (the country word out, to break a collision with the blog index) and two
      openings are changed as well: a sentence describing an online platform listing several
      breeders' litters, which this business is not, and a "fully compliant with DEFRA
      regulations" claim with no inspection or licence on file (LICENCE_CLAIM_PLACEHOLDER, Known
      Issue 7). The London H3 is in the plural for a collision, and the "based in" clause naming
      the former city is gone along with the eight location links it introduced. NO TURNAROUND
      TIME is stated: no file on disk holds one. The recorded refresh delta is the LAYOUT. */}
  <section id="delivery" data-section-label="Collection and delivery">
    <h2>{T(heading('delivery'))}</h2>
    <p>{opening('delivery')}</p>
    <BodyImage asset={nationwide} />

    <h3>{T(node('delivery', 0).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('delivery', 0)}</p>

    <h3>{T(node('delivery', 1).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('delivery', 1)}</p>

    <h3>{T(node('delivery', 2).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      The puppy travels in a secured crate with water and stops for breaks on the way. You are
      told when it leaves here and told again when it is close. The handover is at your door, to
      you, with the paperwork in the same hand. The price is {delivery}, set by the distance from
      {' '}{town} rather than by the dog.
      {' '}<a href="/buy-staffy-puppies-for-sale-uk/">{S('Read why families across the UK choose us')}</a> for
      the longer version of how we work before you book anything.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('delivery', 3).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('delivery', 3)}</p>
    <p>
      Collection in {town} is always the alternative, and it is the one we would gently push you
      towards where the journey is short enough: seeing where a puppy was raised answers most of
      the questions on this page in a single afternoon.
    </p>
    <BodyImage asset={ukFamily} />
  </section>

  {/* 15 adoption-vs-buying — standard, NO PICK. The alternative, stated fairly and named rather
      than dismissed. The H2 and its opening are migrated wording; the opening is
      `verbatim.changed` because "and lifelong support" is an open-ended commitment with no term
      and nothing on disk behind it. NO REHOMING SEARCH IS LINKED (`dropped.links`): sending a
      reader to a live listing from a page that sells puppies is a referral we cannot keep
      accurate. The recorded refresh delta is the CONTAINER. */}
  <section id="adoption-vs-buying" data-section-label="Rehoming or buying">
    <h2>{T(heading('adoption-vs-buying'))}</h2>
    <p>{opening('adoption-vs-buying')}</p>
    <BodyImage asset={adoptionInfographic} />

    <h3>{T(node('adoption-vs-buying', 0).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      A dog that needs a home, at a fraction of the cost, from people who will tell you honestly
      what they know about it and what they do not. Staffies are among the most commonly rehomed
      dogs in this country, and a reader who ends up at a rescue has still made a good decision.
      We would rather say that than leave it out.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('adoption-vs-buying', 1).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      Known parentage, screened parents, a puppy raised in a house rather than met as an adult,
      and somebody to ring afterwards who knew the dog first.
      {' '}<a href="https://www.thekennelclub.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Kennel Club, the registry our litters are registered with</a> is
      where our paperwork comes from. A registration says who the parents were and nothing beyond
      that — it is not a test result and not a grade, which is why the DNA certificates are asked
      for separately.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* 16 owner-review — reviews, picked style S1 as the BED and as the MODE (one review given
      room, `mode: 'single'`, which is one of the axes `RENDERED_AXES.reviews` lists): the pick
      decides how the block is drawn and it is read off the StyleDef rather than hard-coded.
      WHICH review is the record's own sentence inside `record_hash` — entry 3, Rachel L. of
      London, the only one of the three that speaks to the buying process rather than to the dog.
      The other two slots are not opened, so no REVIEW_PLACEHOLDER is counted here. The recorded
      refresh delta is the DENSITY. */}
  <section id="owner-review" data-section-label="One buyer on the process" class={box('owner-review')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('owner-review'))}</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <Testimonial mode={reviewStyle.layout.mode ?? 'single'} reviews={rachel} />
      <p>
        Everything above is a breeder describing her own process. One family in London, named,
        describing it from the other end, is a different kind of sentence.
      </p>
      <BodyImage asset={reviewsPhoto} />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 17 puppies — puppies, picked style S2 (the two-up grid beside the heading), filtered on
      `status` from data/puppies.json rather than hard-coding a count. The cards' own links are
      grid data and are exempt from link parity (spec §9 amendment 6b). NO per-puppy Offer
      markup — the listing page owns it. The H2 is `verbatim.changed` for its tick glyph. The
      migrated line under it — four dogs and four prices that are not on disk, plus a lifetime
      support claim — is struck by `dropped.prices`, and the grid renders the six dogs that
      exist. The recorded refresh delta is the LAYOUT. */}
  <section id="puppies" data-section-label="Meet our puppies" class={box('puppies')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('puppies'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">These are the puppies we have now, each with a name, a sex, a colour and a price.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <div class="bl-cards">
        {available.map((p) => <PuppyCard slug={p.slug} />)}
      </div>
      <p>
        <a href="/buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk/">{S('the puppies we have available now')}</a>.
        {' '}<a href="#talk-to-us">Put the {questionWord} questions to us</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 18 questions — faq, picked style S2 (the heading and intro beside the accordion). The
      section's `refresh.note` argues for the accordion in a card with a jump list, which is S3;
      the PICK is S2. Four rows of data/faq.json in the record's order: three are sourced to this
      page and the fourth, the deposit, is data/settings.json's. The accordion's answers sit
      outside this section's word band (amendment 4a). The recorded refresh delta is the
      CONTAINER. */}
  <section id="questions" data-section-label="Questions families ask" class={box('questions')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('questions'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">Four that arrive in almost every first email.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      {/* The section's own words, which the accordion answers do not supply: `board_gate` counts
          an accordion's answers outside the band (amendment 4a), so a section rendering nothing
          but rows reads as having said nothing. No new claim is made here. */}
      <p>
        Every answer below restates something said above it under a heading: nothing is kept
        back for the accordion, and nothing lives only behind a disclosure triangle. Three come
        from first emails; the fourth is the deposit, the one people are least willing to ask
        about.
      </p>
      <Faq items={faqs} />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 19 talk-to-us — standard, NO PICK, and the close. The only ask on the page, and it is that
      the reader turns the list on us before they turn it on anybody else. The two locked prices,
      the refundable deposit and the delivery band are read out of data/price-matrix.json and
      data/settings.json rather than typed. The H2 and the first H3 are migrated wording; two
      openings are `verbatim.changed`, one for a calculator the migrated page did not contain and
      one for a named laboratory and a champion-bloodline claim with nothing on disk behind
      either. NO URGENCY, no countdown and no scarcity. NO FORM: the contact page carries the one
      form the form audit measures, and this section links it. The recorded refresh delta is the
      LAYOUT. */}
  <section id="talk-to-us" data-section-label="Ready to welcome your Blue Staffy">
    <h2>{T(heading('talk-to-us'))}</h2>
    <p>{opening('talk-to-us')}</p>

    <h3>{T(node('talk-to-us', 0).heading)}</h3>
    <p>{nodeOpening('talk-to-us', 0)}</p>

    <h3>{T(node('talk-to-us', 1).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      Every question in the table above, and every row of the comparison under it, is one we have
      answered before and will answer again. Ask them here first, while the stakes are an email,
      and you will know what an unhurried answer sounds like when you hear one somewhere else.
    </p>

    <h3>{T(node('talk-to-us', 2).heading)}</h3>
    <p>
      £{gbp(prices.male_gbp)} for {males}; £{gbp(prices.female_gbp)} for {females}. {deposit}
      reserves whichever you name, and you have it back if you change your mind.
      {' '}{settings.delivery_note} — {delivery} — or collect in {town}.
      {' '}<a href="/uk-blue-staffy-breeders-contact/">{S('Write to us and put the list to us')}</a> —
      name the puppy and say who is at home in the day. Everything comes to {SITE.email}, which
      {' '}{SITE.breeder_name} reads herself between feeds, {hours}. No telephone number is
      published yet. Visitors are welcome.
    </p>

    <h4>{T('The Close Of A Guide Like This Has To Be An Invitation')}</h4>
    <p>
      Not a countdown. A page that has spent two thousand words telling you that pressure is a
      warning sign does not get to apply any at the bottom of it.
    </p>
    <h5>{T('Writing To Us Reserves Nothing')}</h5>
    <p>
      Sending an email holds nothing and joins nothing. A puppy comes off the list when a deposit
      is against its name, and not before.
    </p>
    <h6>{T('Buyer Note: The first thing we ask about is your household')}</h6>
    <p>Not the garden and not the postcode — who is in the house during the day, because that is what this breed notices most.</p>
  </section>

  {/* 20 video-what-to-expect — video, picked style S1 (the player in a card, caption beneath it).
      The section's `refresh.note` argues for the click-to-play thumbnail, which is S3 and is what
      working rule 14 makes the default "unless the breeder picks otherwise" — they picked S1, and
      the PICK beats the note. Working rule 14 on the id: `WuA0yo6HZKE` is the one id data/facts
      records for this page, carried unchanged and kept at the foot of the page where the migrated
      body had it. The VideoObject in the schema above is built from this same block, so the page,
      the schema and the video sitemap describe one id in one spelling. The recorded refresh delta
      is the MOTIF. */}
  <section id="video-what-to-expect" data-section-label="Real footage" class={box('video-what-to-expect')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('video-what-to-expect'))}</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <VideoEmbed
        id={video.id}
        title={video.title}
        caption={video.caption}
        play={videoStyle.layout.play ?? 'iframe'}
      />
      <p>
        No commentary. It is our puppies as they were on the day, which is the one thing a page
        of writing cannot show you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageShell>
